  "result": "I fixed the keyset cursor in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`. The cause was that `keysetPredicate` resumed a page with `sortColumn < cursorSortValue` alone. Rows that shared the boundary row's timestamp were excluded from the next page, even though they were not yet shown. Bulk imports and bulk audit or notification bursts create many rows with the same `createdAt`, which is why gradually created lists paged correctly.\n\nThe predicate now resumes on the full `(sort, id)` ordering the queries already use: `sortColumn < v OR (sortColumn = v AND idColumn < id)`. Every repository that uses `keysetPredicate` (issues, projects, members, comments, notifications, activity, search) already passes an `idColumn`, and its `ORDER BY` already sorts by `id` descending as the tiebreaker. The org-scoping filters are unchanged.\n\nI haven't run the test suite. The existing test in `tests/repositories/issue-repository.test.ts` covers paging, but it may not include equal timestamps.",
